# Story 44: Toggling Raw Mode (##raw) (35s)
# Hook: Need raw mode without an interactive program? ##raw flips it on and off by hand.
# Duration: 35s
# Source: story-044-toggling-raw-mode.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Need raw mode without an interactive program? ##raw flips it on and off by hand.

[00:03.0 --> 00:07.0]
Raw mode usually engages automatically -- but you can control it directly.

[00:07.0 --> 00:13.0]
Double-Escape to rysh mode, where ## system commands live.

[00:13.0 --> 00:22.0]
Type ##raw to turn raw mode on manually. Now keystrokes are forwarded as raw bytes to the PTY -- handy for stubborn programs Rysh didn't auto-detect.

[00:22.0 --> 00:30.0]
##raw is a toggle. Press Ctrl+O to step out to prefix mode, then run ##raw again to turn it back off.

[00:30.0 --> 00:35.0]
One command, full manual control over the interactive terminal.

